diff --git a/paper/main.typ b/paper/main.typ
index a99206c3..c602da23 100644
--- a/paper/main.typ
+++ b/paper/main.typ
@@ -1316,0 +1317,75 @@ recurrence.
+#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[Delayed learning and the composition frontier]
+
+A short run can miss learning altogether. In the instrumented one-step
+E97 run, validation accuracy stays near zero for roughly 20,000 updates
+(2.93% at update 20,000), then follows a clean S-curve to 97.85% at
+57,000 updates. This silent-then-ignite signature explains why a shallow
+training horizon can read as failure. It describes the learning curve,
+not its mechanism. Replaying the earlier stopping rule would have ended
+this successful run at update 10,000.
+
+The growth curriculum therefore uses an open horizon, advances only
+at 90% joint validation accuracy, and stops for registered stagnation
+rather than a fixed training budget. Its 100,000-update stage-local
+floor is calibrated against the successful one-step replay, not a
+guarantee of later learning. The plateau streak resets through that
+floor. Two consecutive eligible comparisons of disjoint 2,000-update
+windows must each show both best-validation gain below 0.1 percentage
+points and relative mean-training-loss decrease below 0.1%; the earliest
+stop is update 104,000. Threshold advancement takes priority. Safety
+ceilings remain separate stop reasons; none fired in these six runs.
+
+The scratch models retain the nominal 8 M configurations above, matched
+learning rate 1e-3 and seeds 0/1/2, using Schedule-Free AdamW, fresh
+procedural training and frozen validation pools. The planned stages are
+4, 8, 16, 32, 64 and 128 drivers, carrying weights, optimizer and training
+RNG between stages. All six learned solutions stopped by the registered
+stagnation rule at the initial four-driver stage, so no later stage was
+entered. E97 stopped at 190,000/104,000/104,000 updates and GDN2 at
+324,000/372,000/204,000. Final joint validation accuracies were
+25.15/25.00/24.95% for E97 and 75.00/74.80/50.05% for GDN2 in seed
+order: ranges of 24.95–25.15% and 50.05–75.00%. Every final checkpoint
+had terminal accuracy 0/512. The suffix-only reference remains 0.026874%
+for initialization plus a proper driver suffix with at least two omitted
+drivers; it does not bound a recurrent model retaining the prefix.
+The uniform marginal loss reference remains 8.221748 nats.
+
+The aggregate fractions suggest a frontier, but do not locate it.
+A frozen positional evaluation of the six existing best-validation
+checkpoints does (#ref(<tab_growth_positions>)). Four drivers follow two
+unscored initial-coordinate tokens, processed causally without target
+feedback. Position 1 requires one application of the nonlinear map.
+
+#expressivity.growth-table <tab_growth_positions>
+
+E97 tracks the first application almost perfectly in every seed
+(511–512/512), then collapses at position 2 (0–10/512). GDN2 tracks
+through position 3 in seeds 0/1 (512/512 and 508/512 there), but only
+through position 2 in seed 2 (4/512 at position 3). The four-application
+position remains unsolved in every run (0–1/512). Here tracking means
+at least the registered 90% accuracy level, not exact correctness.
+The shorthand does not erase partial-coordinate signal: E97 seed 0
+has 338/512 first-coordinate predictions correct at position 2 despite
+only 10/512 joint hits; GDN2 seed 2 has 105/512 first-coordinate
+hits at position 3.
+
+These are pre-existing best-aggregate-validation checkpoints, selected
+by joint accuracy and then loss on ties, not selected anew by position.
+They use the same 512 frozen sequences per seed as training validation,
+not an independent test pool. E97 best seeds 1/2 each have one terminal
+hit, unlike their final checkpoints; isolated hits do not solve the
+fourth application. Full counts, coordinate scores, losses, hashes and
+best-versus-final reconciliation are retained in
+`paper/results/invertible_quadratic/growth/`.
+
+Together, flat full-depth training leaves both architectures near the
+marginal reference, while the progressive-depth protocol reveals a
+composition frontier at its first stage. The learned GDN2 solutions
+chain three sequential applications of the nonlinear map through the
+recurrence in two seeds and two in the third; the learned E97 solutions
+chain one. Neither reaches four. This is a finding about learned
+solutions under this training regime and protocol, not an architectural
+capacity limit or impossibility result, nor an identified internal
+mechanism. The positional receipts, rather than aggregate fractions
+alone, support this high-accuracy-depth reading.
+
